WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:07.256
(DOORBELL RINGING)

2
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.928
Is Riley here?

3
00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.098
Red alert!

4
00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.393
- (ALARM BLARING)
- AUTOMATED VOICE: Boy. Boy.

5
00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:23.397
AUTOMATED VOICE: Boy. Boy. Boy.

6
00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.815
There's a boy in my house.

7
00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.317
I knew she was going skating,
but I thought it was with her friends.

8
00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:28.694
Why is there a boy in my house?

9
00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:31.530
This isn't a date, is it? I'll ask Riley.

10
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:33.949
I don't like this.

11
00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.118
This can't be a date! She's only 12!

12
00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.747
Let's probe, but layer it
with cool words the kids say,

13
00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:41.123
so it's not obvious.

14
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.501
So, what's the dealio with Jordan?

15
00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:48.839
O- M-G, he is awesome-sauce
fo sheezy.

16
00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:49.923
MOM: I'm not playin'.

17
00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:51.800
Did she just say "fo sheezy"?

18
00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.844
I don't understand. What's happening?

19
00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:56.972
Ugh, this is just embarrassing.
I can't. I can't.

20
00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.182
MOM: Holla!

21
00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:02.978
(SNIFFLES)

22
00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:06.231
I know what you're doing here, Jordan.

23
00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:08.650
You don't think that I know what
you know, but I know, you little punk!

24
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.736
He's not good enough for Riley.
No one is!

25
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.071
Go back to jail!

26
00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:14.907
DAD'S ANGER: What are you
looking for, Jordan? Something to steal?

27
00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:16.575
- Like our daughter.
- Should we say something?

28
00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:18.368
No, no, no. He'll be expecting that.

29
00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:21.538
Give him the silent treatment.
He's about to crack, I can feel it.

30
00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:28.670
- (LOUD ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)
- Whoa, dude! Awesome!

31
00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:33.842
Sir, no response.

32
00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:37.221
Two can play at your mind games,
Jordan. Intimidate!

33
00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.307
(INHALES SHARPLY)

34
00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.771
Dude, what's he looking at?

35
00:01:45.855 --> 00:01:47.439
Probably your dumb hat.

36
00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:48.524
(CHUCKLES)

37
00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.775
- Whoa!
- (LAUGHING)

38
00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.860
- (GRUNTS)
- (CRASHING)

39
00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.320
(CHUCKLES)

40
00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:56.573
- Sir, intimidation is failing.
- (SCOFFS)

41
00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.659
Increase the pressure. Engage.

42
00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:03.372
So, Jordan,
what do you like to do for fun?

43
00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.833
I don't know. Stuff.

44
00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.959
Sir, that sounds like backtalk.

45
00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:10.963
(GROANS) That's it! He's outta here!
Give him the boot.

46
00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:12.464
Yes, sir. Launching boot.

47
00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:13.841
(ALARM BLARING)

48
00:02:19.013 --> 00:02:22.558
On my mark. In five, four, three...

49
00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:24.017
Oh...

50
00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:26.562
I play in a band. That's fun.

51
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.439
Wait. We were in a band.

52
00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:35.529
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

53
00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.490
I was in a band, lead guitar.

54
00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.909
Cool. I rock the bass.

55
00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.079
- We played a lot ofAC/DC.
- Yeah, my favorite band is AC/DC.

56
00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.706
- (GASPS)
- What.

57
00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:48.125
Mom, ew, it's not a date.

58
00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:50.127
We're going skating
with a group of friends.

59
00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:53.172
Oh, fun. That'll be off the hook. L-O-L.

60
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:54.381
Stop talking like that!

61
00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:55.465
Wait. Where's Jordan?

62
00:02:55.758 --> 00:02:57.509
Did you leave Jordan with Dad?

63
00:02:57.594 --> 00:02:58.844
Mom! This is so embarrassing.

64
00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:01.054
Riley, your father
would never do any...

65
00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:05.601
(LOUD ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

66
00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.685
Yeah!

67
00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:09.938
- Awesome.
- (CRASHING)

68
00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.149
Bye, Mom. Bye, Dad.

69
00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:14.109
- Have fun.
- Peace out, my homies.

70
00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:17.112
You know, Jordan's a good kid.

71
00:03:17.238 --> 00:03:18.864
You're not so bad yourself.

72
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.450
Sir, the wife has initiated contact.
What do we do?

73
00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.328
This is our chance. Give her the look.

74
00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.001
(SCOFFS) He's making
that stupid face again.

75
00:03:31.127 --> 00:03:32.127
MOM'S ANGER: Ugh.
Should we smack him?

76
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.713
Come on. He's adorable.

77
00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:37.799
There's the signal.

78
00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.468
- (KEYBOARDS CLACKING)
- We are go. Repeat, we are go.

79
00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:43.347
Contact in five, four, three, two...

80
00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:49.228
- (CHEERING)
- (LOUD ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

81
00:03:49.437 --> 00:04:17.422
(EXPLOSION)

82
00:04:22.553 --> 00:04:24.554
(POP MUSIC PLAYING)

83
00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:28.517
I'm good. You guys good?

84
00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:29.726
- Yeah. I'm good.
- Yeah, I'm good here.

85
00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:31.770
- Good.
- (MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

86
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.647
Okay, that's enough.

87
00:04:34.023 --> 00:04:38.735
Ah, yeah.
Um... I'll go fix the table.
